The abundance of dual-cab utes, Norfolk Island pines, low timber post-and-rail park fencing, and a yellow diamond warning sign on the left side of the road strongly point to coastal Australia. The white rear license plates, overcast temperate skies, and coastal marine rescue building with a radio tower at the end of the car park are characteristic of a headland or breakwater reserve along the New South Wales or Victorian coast.

